tern. The robot is guarding a door, and you've been trying to convince the robot to let you through. You need to find the maintenance key (explicit appeal process) or the building manager (supervisor/elected official), not argue with the robot's programming. Does that make more sense? I'm not on the side of the bureaucrats here—I'm on your side, trying to give you the cheat codes.
